From cf57e517ed80e3a990784516288bfc175d112d88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 18:14:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] prosetheme: themes for the machine, applied from one file

A theme is a window decorator, the system's colours and the desktop's
wallpaper; prosetheme lists the NAME.theme files in
/boot/system/data/prose/themes and ~/config/settings/prose/themes and
applies one: colours through set_ui_color(), the decorator as setdecor
does, the wallpaper as the Backgrounds preferences write it (the
attribute on the Desktop folder, then B_RESTORE_BACKGROUND_IMAGE to
Tracker). Every part is kept by the server that owns it, so a theme
survives a restart; the name is kept for --list and --current. A key a
theme leaves out keeps its value, so a theme may be partial.

Three ship: Prose Light (the paper wallpaper, a light frame with the
round buttons at the left), Prose Dark (the ink wallpaper, a charcoal
frame, the system's dark palette), and Classic (the yellow tab and the
default colours a new machine has). All three list every colour, so
switching back restores everything.

In the prose_portal package with the daemon: the host offers them in
View > Theme and applies one through the portal.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Prose-Patch: 0073-prosetheme-themes-for-the-machine-applied-from-one-file.patch e08c44a9e4dea7c974cd8d2c0704daa7155f317e05e1697b1afc2b9e0d8e4ed1
